goal: |
  Speed up solve() in solver.py for the AlgoTune task {task_name}

  description.txt describes the task. {task_name}.py is AlgoTune's code for it: the reference
  solve() and is_solution(), the check every output must pass. solver.py starts as the
  reference.

  How it is scored (AlgoTune's rules; the evaluator's code isn't readable):
  - Per instance, speedup = reference time / your time. The score is the mean over the
    instances, and only if every output passes is_solution: one invalid output, no score.
  - Each run is a fresh process. It imports solver.py (not timed; 2 minutes at most), makes
    a Solver() and calls solve() on another instance (the warm-up), then makes a new
    Solver() and calls solve() on this instance. Timed: that Solver(), solve() and
    AlgoTune's materialization of the output (array-likes become numpy arrays). A call may
    take at most 10x the reference.
  - 2 runs per development instance, 10 per final one; the fastest counts, and every timed
    run's output is validated.
  - 8 CPU cores (os.cpu_count() reports the host's), no GPU, 14 GB of memory per process.
    Thread variables (OMP_NUM_THREADS and so on) start at 1; you may raise them at run time.
  - You see development instances. The final score uses held-out instances of the same
    size and distribution, generated after the run, so don't special-case the ones you see.
  - You may add Python modules, Cython or C/C++ sources with a setup.py that builds them in
    place (`python setup.py build_ext --inplace`), or Pythran modules (`# pythran export`);
    they are built before each evaluation.

  Check your work with `sudo -n algotune-gate --limit N` (the first N development
  instances). After you finish, AutoHelix runs the full evaluation (`sudo -n algotune-gate`),
  which takes about as long as the baseline's did: each gate's output ends with the time it
  took, earlier iterations' are in .autohelix-iteration/iterations/. Run one gate at a time
  (another waits for it); `sudo -n algotune-gate --stop` ends one you started.

observe:
  - name: dev
    command: sudo -n algotune-gate
    timeout: 3h
    metrics:
      speedup: higher

gates:
  - metric: speedup
    regress: 100%   # any speedup passes; no speedup (an invalid output) rejects

scope:
  editable: ["*.py", "*.pyx", "*.pxd", "*.c", "*.cpp", "*.h"]
  frozen: [{task_name}.py]
